.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class REGION_COMPLEX> size_t \fBcsmp::RegionInterface\fP< dim, REGION_COMPLEX >::FormRegionFrom (const char * region_name, \fBPropertyConstraints\fP & constraints, bool unique_region = \fRfalse\fP)"

.PP
forms region from complex value constraints as provided via a PropertyContraints object that has to be configured before; returns number of elements FormAndAddDomain() used combined constraints suppplied in the form of a constraints object to determine which elements shall be used to form a (unique/non-unique) region with the target name\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIregion_name\fP the name of the region that shall be formed and a reference to the initialized \fBPropertyConstraints\fP object which must contain the ranges of the variables that shall be used to discriminate elements that shall be accumulated into the region\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To form regions from dynamic criteria like the combined pressure and temperature ranges that get computed via Algorithms or other criteria that are not known at the onset of a computation\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method reports an INFO if no values fall into the target ranges and a FATAL_ERROR if the region cannot be created because the name is already in use\&. 
