.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class REGION_COMPLEX> size_t \fBcsmp::RegionInterface\fP< dim, REGION_COMPLEX >::FormRegionsFromPropertyValues (const char * prop, std::set< std::string > & region_names)"

.PP
treats the values of the property as discrete, forming one region per value and returning their names into the set; returns number of regions RegionsFromPropertyValues() defines one region for each value of the target property\&. The user will be prompted to assign a name to each region as these are being created\&. The names of successfully created regions are returned into the list argument\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIprop\fP the property on the basis of whose variations the region regions will be defined\&.
.RE
.PP
The names of the newly created regions are returned into an STL set which uses the less<> functional to order the names alphabetically\&. If the set is not empty, it will be erased before the region names are stored within it\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Thus far, the method only handles scalar variables\&. Since there is always just one property value per element, the regions will be unique\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
RegionsFromPropertyValues() is useful if the desired subregions of a model coincide with changes of a specific property\&. Clearly, one does not want to apply this method on a continuously changing property, since it might produce as many Regions as there are finite-elements in the mesh\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method is interactive and will prompt the user for the names of the regions which are created in the course of its execution\&. 
