.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class REGION_COMPLEX> size_t \fBcsmp::RegionInterface\fP< dim, REGION_COMPLEX >::PartitionRegionIntoContiguousSubRegions (const char * region)"

.PP
finds disconnected subregions in region, dividing it into these\&. The new subregion are numbered and their total # is returned Breaks non-contiguous Regions into contiguous subregions that carry the name of the region but have a number as suffix to their name to denote the partition\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The method returns the number of subgregions that were created\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
The master region that was successfully partitioned is removed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIregion\fP The name of the region that may be non-contiguous\&. If so, new sbregions will be created to the name of which integers will be appended that correspond to the number of subdomains that are created in this process\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The method returns the number of contiguous subdomains which it created\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The method uses the element neighbor information to perform floodfills as required until all member elements are partitioned\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To automatically partition regions that consist of a multitude of non-contiguous model subdomains so that the latter can be addressed individually in computations\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method will report if the region is already contiguous in which case no changes are made\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
this method cannot be applied to the region model or the master region 
.RE
.PP

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class REGION_COMPLEX> size_t \fBcsmp::RegionInterface\fP< dim, REGION_COMPLEX >::PartitionRegionIntoContiguousSubRegions_Bromage (const char * region)"
ANDREW BROMAGE VERSION

.PP
Breaks non-contiguous \fBRegion\fP into contiguous subregions that carry the name of the original region, but have a number as a suffix to their name to distinguish each partition\&. All elements and the original region are retained, but the original region is moved into the non-unique regions storage\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The method returns the number of subgregions that were created, if any\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIregion\fP The name of the region that may be non-contiguous\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The method uses the union-find algorithm, using element neighbours to determine which parts of it are contiguous\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
this method is implemented using \fBUnionFind\fP as opposed to standard floodfill operations\&. This might cause performance issues\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To partition regions into contiguous subdomains such as fractures so that these can be processed one-by-one by various algorithms\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method will report if the region is contiguous to start with\&. In this case no subregions will be created\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
it makes no sense to apply this method to region "Model" or complex non-unique regions\&.
.RE
.PP
